// Subjugator-class heavy cruiser (the Malevolence), measured from the STL file
// the user supplied (Malevolence.stl, "Converted by 3D Object Converter"; no
// author or licence came with it). Ship frame: x from the stern (0) to the bow
// (4,845 m, the canon length; the model is scaled uniformly, 3.18886 m per model
// unit, with the file's +Y (bow) to x, +Z (up) to y and +X to z), y up from the
// lowest point, z to starboard. The hull starts at the stern hood (hull.start,
// x 470.5 m; aft of it there are only the nozzle tubes and the spar) and is
// fitted station by station (30 warship-octagon stations): the hood over the
// nozzles, the long fuselage, the head (the shoulders and the
// cannon section, without the cannon housings, the ring ports and the dorsal
// blister), the upper body over the split prow's mouth and the upper prow to
// the bow tip; the head's side trench (y 202-342 m) is carved back as a hull
// trench. Structures measured from the model: the stern spar (the swept trunk,
// the main bridge head on top and the communications boom aft of it), the
// fourteen nozzle tubes, the raised dorsal band, the armoured dorsal
// command-centre blister (plate), the vent stacks and antenna masts,
// the ventral posts, the four cross-barred ring ports, the upper-lip wings and
// the lower jaw, and the hyper-ion cannon housings (spherical caps, R 280.5 m
// about |z| 362.1) with their collar rings (r 155.6-179.4 m, |z| 605-648).
// The two hyper-ion cannons ('hion', fixed 310.8 m x 250 m) sit at x 3060.4,
// y 289.4, |z| 546.2 with their dished faces at |z| 671.2 (the ship's beam),
// wired to the spherical main reactor amidships between them (324 m across, sized
// so the whole load, guns included, recharges at the full rate), as the cutaway
// shows; the corridor between the reactor and each cannon is kept clear.
// The existing 20 heavy, 20 medium, 200 light and 400 PD turret seats now
// use the spherical Mon Calamari family. Five hundred more single 34 TT balls
// replace the former casemates in the trench walls and fuselage flank rows.
// Ten proton-torpedo launchers and two heavy tractor stations remain. The batteries are
// mounted in one pass under a locked cache and frozen structure meshes, which
// keeps the build time down; droid-control automation holds the crew at the
// canon 23,530.
// The main bridge is the head at the top of the stern spar, the tall fin-like
// tower: on screen it is where Grievous commands the ship ("Rising
// Malevolence", "Shadow of Malevolence", "Destroy Malevolence"), and
// Wookieepedia's Legends article (from The Clone Wars: The Visual Guide and
// those episodes) puts the command centre in "a multi-storied structure at the
// top" of the tower near the stern, beside the communications array
